A second GS memory on the same device: pages copied from the first, and the two drawing in turns

A second GS memory (DW5XL issue 049, fact-finding 2026-11-11): GSInterface::copy_pages_from(source, pages)
copies pages of another GSInterface on the same device into this one's VRAM on the GPU (every slice in use,
each page's flag, the current CLUT), so extra pictures can be drawn apart from the game's GS.

Two GS memories drawing in turns (DW5XL issue 049, amendment v3.7): each keeps its own work open while the
other draws, so that where the turns fall does not show in a picture (what a render pass draws depends on where
it ends). Granite waits for every open command buffer of the device when a frame context ends, and
GSRenderer::flush_submit ends one. With GSInterface::set_frame_context_hold(hold) a flush leaves the frame
context alone while `hold` says true; the caller makes it say so while another GS memory of the device has open
command buffers (GSInterface::has_open_command_buffers). The frame context is only where the device frees
things.

The page tracker says and sets whether a page's memory may hold super-sampled content
(PageTracker::page_may_super_sample, set_page_may_super_sample): that is each page's flag, copied with the page.

The rollback point of the earlier version of this patch was removed on 2026-11-13 (DW5XL issue 049, M3).

Applies on top of 0001-0006.

